{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And it was told to the king of Egypt.</b> He sent escorts (אִיקְטוֹרִין) with them, and when three days — the time they had fixed to go and return — had passed, and they saw that they were not returning to Egypt, they came and told Pharaoh on the fourth day. On the fifth and the sixth they pursued after them; on the night of the seventh they went down into the sea; in the morning they said the song — and that is the seventh day of Passover. Therefore we read the song on the seventh day." "<b>And it was turned.</b> Turned from what it had been — for he had said to them, ״קוּמוּ צְּאוּ מִתּוֹךְ עַמִּ״ (Exodus 12), and the heart of his servants turned, for previously they had been saying to him, ״עַד מָתַי יִהְיֶה זֶה לָנוּ לְמוֹקֵשׁ״ (Exodus 10), and now they turned to pursue them for the wealth they had lent them." "<b>From serving us.</b> From serving us."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "אִיקְטוֹרִין is from Greek ἐπίσκοποι or similar, meaning guards/escorts; left transliterated as in the original."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:09.212481683Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}